{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
You are my [F]Shepherd.
I'll want for [Bb]nothing.
You make me [F]lie down
In pastures of [C]green.
Beside still [Dm]waters
And down paths of [Bb]righteous[Gm7]ness
All for your [F]name's sake,
[C]Shepherd, you [F]lead.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
You re[Bb]store my soul. You re[Dm7]store my soul.
Surely good[F]ness and mercy will [Csus]fol[C]low.
And I will [Dm]dwell in the house [Bb]of the Lord for[F]ever,
There with my [C]Shepherd, [Bb]Shepherd [Gm7]of my [F]soul.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Even when [F]walking
Down through the [Bb]valley
There in death's [F]shadow
No evil I'll [C]fear.
You're always [Dm]with me.
Your rod and staff [Bb]comfort [Gm7]me.
Jesus, my [F]Shepherd,
[C]You're always [F]near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge}
[F]You set a table before [Gm7]me,
With my [F/A]enemies all around.
[Dm]Let your anointing fall on [C]me.
Let my [F]cup overflow with your [Bb]pow'r.
{end_of_bridge}
